; Transfer matching (plan 35): a small household journal whose bank feeds are
; imported one file per account. Every transfer between them lands on a
; clearing account under `transfers`, one half from each feed, and Ledgeline's
; Find Matches pairs the halves up.
;
; Read as of 2027-01-31 (the docs screenshots pin that day). What it holds:
;
; - two pairs already linked (`match:`), shown as one transfer row each;
; - six clear pairs not yet linked, one crossing the year (Dec 31 → Jan 2);
; - two $200 transfers four days apart whose halves tie (both "check");
; - a pair rejected with `nomatch:`, each half pairing elsewhere instead;
; - a $250 transfer to savings whose other half never arrived (in transit);
; - a link broken by an edit after linking (the amounts no longer cancel);
; - a bill-pay debit paying two bills, suggested as one combination, and one
;   whose bills sum to it two ways, not suggested (matching/billpay.journal).
;
; web/docs-screenshots/matching.docs.ts and the engine's fixture test
; (crates/ledgeline-server/tests/match_fixture.rs) read this file. Change the
; test's expectations with it.

account assets:checking                 ; type: C
account assets:savings                  ; type: C
account liabilities:amex                ; type: L
account income:salary                   ; type: R
account expenses:groceries              ; type: X
account expenses:dining                 ; type: X
account expenses:utilities              ; type: X
account expenses:contractors            ; type: X
account equity:opening                  ; type: E
account transfers                       ; clearing:
account transfers:internal-bank
account transfers:creditcard-payment
account transfers:billpay

include matching/checking.journal
include matching/savings.journal
include matching/amex.journal
include matching/billpay.journal
